      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. The test verifies that `withNano()` throws `IllegalArgumentException` when given a value equal to 1,000,000,000 (which equals `NANOS_PER_SECOND`, the exclusive upper bound). I'll improve understandability by:\n\n1. Renaming the cryptic variable `taiInstant0`\n2. Replacing the noisy auto-generated comment `// Undeclared exception!` with a clear intent comment\n3. Using a named constant for the boundary value\n4. Removing the empty `//` comment inside the catch blockThe improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version extracts the boundary value into a named constant `ONE_BILLION_NANOS`, renames `taiInstant0` to `instant`, and replaces the auto-generated `// Undeclared exception!` noise with a clear comment explaining why `withNano(1_000_000_000)` is invalid."
